"""Pre-review expansion of already registered descriptive evidence; no new inference."""
import shutil
import study as r
def main():
    names=['MANUSCRIPT.md','METHODS.md','RESULTS.md','supplements/A08.md','supplements/A09.md']
    backup=r.HERE/'reports_before_expansion';backup.mkdir(exist_ok=False)
    old={}
    for n in names:
        p=backup/n;p.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);shutil.copy2(r.HERE/n,p);old[n]=r.sha(r.HERE/n)
    r.save(r.HERE/'artifact_expansion_registration.json',{'utc':r.datetime.now(r.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'before_final_review':True,'source_sha256':r.sha(r.HERE/'finalize_reporting.py'),'preimage_sha256':old,'purpose':'Expose all already registered probe/rate results and mixed/negative controls in the main draft, retain pre-review text; no new model, test, selection or changed numeric result','final_access':False})
    methods=(r.HERE/'METHODS.md').read_text()+'\nRecording calendar dates and independent anatomical assignments were not independently established in this track. Source acquisition provenance is inherited through the frozen manifests and original custody/QC receipts. Native receipt legacy labels are annotated in NATIVE_SCOPE_ANNOTATION.md; actual authorized scope is the hashed Development A/B inputs. The shared-ACL execution failure and all24 completed controls were retained; remaining controls used three independently provisioned role resources, with unchanged source data, seeds,999replicates and direct-versus-cached prediction/score parity checks.\n'
    results=(r.HERE/'RESULTS.md').read_text()+'\n## Probe, rate and mixed-control interpretation\n\n[Complete per-mouse probe assessment](PROBE_DEPENDENCE.md) reports every selected shared-probe value and every available leave-probe-out range. Maximum within-mouse shifts from primary are0.09764899 (own),0.01908291 (population),0.01053225 (stimulus/time) and0.09438581 (combined) nats per nominal unit-bin. These shifts can exceed the corresponding cohort-average regional contrast; probe/selected-population dependence is a substantive limitation. They are not extra independent replicates or a basis for choosing a favorable probe.\n\n[Training-rate matching audit](RATE_MATCHING.md) shows22–30 matched pairs per mouse and residual maximum absolute log-rate ratios up tolog(2). Matching is therefore approximate. The16-unit view reverses the stimulus/time and combined mean contrast signs relative to primary. Population mean direction remains negative across the five main views, but this does not overcome the corrected primary p0.0693 or establish probe-independent anatomy.\n\nTemporal redistribution retains substantial own-history pooled gain: reference0.02495026 versus observed0.03110484. Thus own-history gain alone is not a pure within-trial temporal-dependence metric; preserved trial-count heterogeneity and conditioning are viable contributors. The temporal references for own/population/combined differ from observed under the conditional tests, while the stimulus/time temporal reference exceeds observed. Order disruption increases the own/population/combined pooled gains, and bin-label disruption increases the population gain. These mixed and negative controls preclude a simple universal feature hierarchy. Condition/bin controls detect some pooled context prediction without corrected regional context support. All contrasts and controls remain reported; no favorable control changes the nonsignificant primary conclusion.\n'
    paper=(r.HERE/'MANUSCRIPT.md').read_text();a=paper.index('## 2. Methods\n\n')+len('## 2. Methods\n\n');b=paper.index('## 3. Results\n\n');paper=paper[:a]+methods.replace('# Frozen methods and interpretation\n\n','')+'\n\n'+paper[b:];a=paper.index('## 3. Results\n\n')+len('## 3. Results\n\n');b=paper.index('### Figures\n\n');paper=paper[:a]+results.replace('# Complete exploratory Development results\n\n','')+'\n\n'+paper[b:]
    for n,text in [('METHODS.md',methods),('RESULTS.md',results),('MANUSCRIPT.md',paper)]: (r.HERE/n).write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
    for n in ('supplements/A08.md','supplements/A09.md'):
        p=r.HERE/n;p.write_text(p.read_text()+'\nFull registered probe/rate numerical assessments: [PROBE_DEPENDENCE.md](../PROBE_DEPENDENCE.md) and [RATE_MATCHING.md](../RATE_MATCHING.md). Mixed controls and all sensitivity sign changes are explicitly discussed in the final RESULTS/MANUSCRIPT. See IMPLEMENTATION_ERRATA and NATIVE_SCOPE_ANNOTATION for preserved execution defects and scope annotation.\n',encoding='utf-8')
    r.save(r.HERE/'artifact_expansion_result.json',{'final_artifact_sha256':{n:r.sha(r.HERE/n) for n in names},'scientific_numeric_results_changed':False,'new_tests':0,'new_fits':0,'final_access':False})
    print('FINAL_DESCRIPTIVE_REPORTING_COMPLETE')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
